**Proposition 161.2 (Continuity and target boundaries).** Theorem 161.1
is a pointwise comparison on the entire original domain. Its proof does
not assert continuous gluing between the Section 160 section on $P$ and
the residual formula of Theorem 113.3. Its atomic output rules have TV
distance one from each unchanged nonatomic $\mu_\xi$ and do not certify
acquisition accuracy against those targets.

**Proof.** The two branches supply existence at the same cap. No equality
of their allocations on their common boundary was required or proved,
so continuity of a glued allocation does not follow. All emitted tapes
are in a finite set of marks in $B_1$; this set has full mass for the
output law and zero mass for a nonatomic target. It therefore gives TV
one, and the unchanged consumer is unknown on those marks. $\square$

